WEBVTT

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:16.490
<b>It was all smoke and mirrors! 

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:16.990
<b>Cult Leader</b>

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:17.160
<b>Fled Overseas</b>

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.070
Soon.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:30.460
Soon, I'll have it... I'll have it all.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.750
<i>Tonight's the night!</i>

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.680
<i>Tonight, we'll have Refloat Waterfront,</i>

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.280
<i>an unprecedented projection mapping event</i>

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.770
<i>to restore the submerged district.</i>

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.910
<i>I'm your reporter, who's already super excited,</i>

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:45.600
<b>Shinmei Amu-chan
Reporting Live</b>

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:45.600
<b>Above Tokyo</b>

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.600
<i>Shinmei Amu!</i>

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.160
Thank you, Amu-san.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:49.270
<i>Sure!</i>

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:52.940
So what's in store for us at this event?

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.200
Take a look at this.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:58.910
First, mist machines installed at each 
station on the big loop line

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:02.250
will create a massive mid-air mist screen.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.120
When the clock strikes midnight,

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:07.640
special trains at all the 
loop-line stations will project

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.840
the light of restoration over the district.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.830
On that starry night screen, we'll see...

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:17.550
<b>This is just an image of what's expected. 
It may not reflect what will actually be shown.</b>

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.690
And thus, the Babylon System

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:24.020
turned to terror...

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:35.650
<i>In response to an increase in heinous crimes,</i>

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:40.030
<i>a new movement is picking up steam in police 
and security forces around the world.</i>

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:46.040
<i>This is the story of the services 
performed by ACTIVE in Japan.</i>

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:59.860
<b>File 10: The Invisible Conqueror</b>

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:13.400
Huh? A password?

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.960
<b>From: ARLM 
To: Bird 

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.610
"Zion," maybe?

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.260
Are you kidding me?

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:26.430
What do you mean, this is the end?

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:29.380
You'd better not be expecting 
to get out of this scot-free.

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:32.560
Hey, don't ignore me, jackass!

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:35.190
Why don't you say something, huh?

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:43.860
Th-Thank you...

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:47.180
Thank you so much.

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:56.100
Nice to meet you, Mythos.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.180
So you're Bird?

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.070
Yeah. What was that just now?

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:04.440
My "big sister" in my twenty-seventh 
fake family, which I'm disbanding today.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.950
Fake families? On a monthly rotation?

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:08.970
Good guess.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:12.100
This is the thirty-second floor, after all.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.540
Anyway, playtime is over.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:19.540
She snapped, thinking I wasn't going to 
pay her father's big loan anymore.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.420
So you decided to pay off the loan, at least?

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:26.820
I dislike unnecessary trouble.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:30.250
It would be idiotic to get injured here.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:38.760
The desert, huh?

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:40.280
You like the desert?

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:43.430
Yes, it's sanitary.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:47.930
By the way, isn't the password at 
the entrance an Atbash cipher?

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:50.600
Was "Zion" intentional irony?

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:54.070
I thought you, of all people, would understand.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:01.780
So, regarding the string of 
incidents since last month,

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:08.030
the laptop of the comatose suspect now 
undergoing treatment, Doumoto Kakeru,

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:10.870
contained files such as how-to's 
for modifying Willwears.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:17.480
I had the Willwear you wanted 
transported to the location we discussed.

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:18.460
Thank you.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:24.700
When you decrypted this and 
answered my call a year ago,

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:26.160
my heart skipped a beat.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:29.520
"Planning to execute the most 
entertaining crime of all time.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:30.890
Looking for partners."

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:33.560
I want to see it soon.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:38.070
You said you would become my 
best partner, did you not?

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:39.000
Yes.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:41.330
Then do this for me.

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:42.870
Option 5?

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:45.110
Fine, it'll be fun.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:47.390
Then let's be even more careful

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:51.280
and delete each other's 
information from the cloud.

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:55.160
Yes, so we can become conquerors.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:58.460
<b>Metropolitan Police Department 
Tokyo Airport Police Station</b>

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:59.240
I have a new lead on the attempted 
bombing of the airplane!

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:02.850
A mechanic who resigned right after 
the incident confessed to letting

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:05.420
a third party into the hangar after 
the pre-flight maintenance.

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:08.180
And that individual rigged the plane?

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:12.460
Yes. The mechanic had suffered 
huge investment losses,

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:14.220
so the generous bribe blinded him.

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:16.270
Any connections to Logos?

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:21.100
His computer was trashed, so there's no 
clear-cut evidence connecting him to Logos.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:22.110
However...

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.070
However?

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:25.780
The description of the saboteur

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:28.820
is basically a dead ringer for 
the boy in the hospital.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.910
So we have a link to Logos?

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:31.820
Great!

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:32.970
But...

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:35.600
The office also told me this,

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:38.500
but wouldn't continuing the investigation 
overstep our bounds?

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:41.460
Each incident's been assigned 
to a specific precinct...

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:42.560
It'll be fine.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:44.420
I have that sorted out.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:50.050
<i>So we're looking forward to tonight's event!</i>

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:54.460
<i>It's sure to light a fire under the Tokyo 
waterfront reconstruction efforts.</i>

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.730
<b>Incoming Call</b>

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.730
<b>Accept              Reject</b>

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.220
President?

00:06:58.630 --> 00:06:59.660
Hello?

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:01.270
Sorry to bother you on your day off.

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:03.270
Can I see you today?

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.650
Oh, I'm free... Why?

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:08.140
There's something I want to tell you.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:09.860
I'll be waiting in the student council room.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:11.400
Oh, okay.

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:13.200
Then I'll see you later.

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:18.250
What should I wear?

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:20.790
Yes, that works.

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:22.360
I'll let you handle the legwork.

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:24.920
Oh, this is a huge help.

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:26.680
Same here.

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:30.380
Many people react negatively 
when we take any action.

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.730
<i>Refloat Waterfront!</i>

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:36.300
<i>Here, in the capital city of Tokyo, 
a new era will begin tonight.</i>

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:39.840
According to the suspects' statements,

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:42.920
they all received an e-mail 
from Logos out of the blue.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.610
The specifics were different,

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:49.210
but each message contained
a specific reference

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:53.880
to what the suspect wanted at the time 
or how the suspect could wreak havoc.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:56.340
Each message contained a unique link

00:07:56.340 --> 00:08:00.660
that gave the suspect access to a special site.

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:04.330
The e-mails bounced through 
several overseas servers,

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:05.920
and the addresses were all different.

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:07.720
We don't know where they were sent from.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:12.340
And the site is inaccessible, 
except through the e-mail links.

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:15.530
Also, we don't know how Logos

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:17.840
determined what the suspects desired.

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:19.350
Did they just cast a wide net?

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:20.760
That's not possible.

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:25.310
In Fukamura's case, they even asked 
if he wanted to meet Shinmei Amu.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:30.410
I doubt Doumoto, AKA 
the Fisherman, was the leader.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:32.490
Remember what he said?

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:36.780
I'm going to have my revenge... on them...

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:39.600
There has to be another... Maybe two?

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:40.500
Huh?

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:42.970
T-To the police in Takanawa?

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:48.410
Hey! Thanks for coming, Hinata-kun.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:49.770
N-No problem.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:54.280
What did you want to talk to me about?

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:59.260
What's "I love you" in Latin?

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:00.120
Huh?

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:04.480
U-Um, "te amo."

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:05.660
Correct.

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:10.920
How about "I want your lip," then?

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:13.060
L-Lip?

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:15.160
Take your time.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:16.900
O-Okay.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:20.830
This is, um...

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:23.250
It's not like we're doing anything wrong—

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:28.250
You're Hachijou Tomoki-kun, 
the one who contacted us, correct?

00:09:28.650 --> 00:09:30.960
Yes, that's me.

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:33.800
Would you come with us 
to the Takanawa station?

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:36.580
Yes, gladly.

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:38.220
P-President?

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:42.220
I am the leader of the 
criminal organization Logos.

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:44.640
I'm known as Bird.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:48.540
No way...

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:57.610
He's Kouki Education Academy's 
student council president.

00:09:57.850 --> 00:10:00.240
He's the student who wrote all those papers

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:02.550
about Willwear incidents, isn't he?

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:05.250
His statements all check out.

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:08.580
Seriously? This kid's the leader of Logos?

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:11.710
He knew all the confidential information. 
We have to believe it.

00:10:12.970 --> 00:10:14.950
Why did you decide to turn yourself in?

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:17.470
Because there's nothing more to do.

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:19.390
What do you mean?

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:22.600
I wanted to see something interesting,

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:24.590
something I'd never seen before.

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:28.220
That's why you were having Willwears 
run around? To have fun?

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:33.640
I suppose, in that sense, I didn't exactly 
meet everyone's expectations.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:37.910
So you're saying you did it because it was fun, 
but now that you're bored, you'll stop?

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:40.530
I recognize that voice. I've met you before.

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:43.090
Then maybe you were the final straw.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.690
With amazing people like you in Unit 8,

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:49.620
I thought I couldn't possibly escape.

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:52.380
I've never met you.

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:55.710
You're the one who saved Hinata-kun.

00:10:57.150 --> 00:11:00.180
Actually, I caused that incident

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:03.210
so that I could collect data on you,

00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:06.140
using the school's security cameras.

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:09.440
Do you even care that you 
involved other students?

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:11.940
Excuse me.

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:15.750
Chief Yamabuki, we have orders to 
transport the suspect to main HQ.

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:17.230
We're to take custody.

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:20.530
Understood.

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:27.830
Sis!

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:31.150
Boss, please take your sister home.

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:33.550
We'll go back to Kichijouji.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:43.490
<b>If you see anything suspicious, call 110.
Let's prevent terrorism!</b>

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:38.210
What a surprise, huh?

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:43.490
<b>We're waiting for your tips! Woof!</b>

00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:40.810
I'm still making sense of it.

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:45.260
What will happen to him?

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:47.320
Main HQ has taken over.

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:51.930
It's not true that he's the leader of Logos, right?

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:56.570
I might end up having to look into it.

00:11:57.990 --> 00:12:01.580
I've been keeping this secret from you 
all this time, but I'm Unit 8's head.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:09.280
Wh-Why is everyone lying to me?

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:23.110
Goodbye, fake Emily.

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:29.720
Guess that's one case down for the count.

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:32.900
I heard Logos is finished now?

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:35.140
Yeah, pretty much.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:37.480
I'm not sure how I feel about that.

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:38.610
Yeah...

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:42.310
Still, it's not like we're out of a job.

00:12:42.310 --> 00:12:44.780
That's right! You're so right!

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:45.950
Yes, it's Funasaka.

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:48.200
Unit 8 will continue to strive to 
stamp out all Willwear crime!

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:48.200
What?

00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:52.210
Okay, I understand.

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:55.080
Who was it?

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:56.260
Main headquarters.

00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:58.670
So they want us to look into it, after all?

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:01.180
No, Unit 8 has been disbanded.

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:01.920
Huh?!

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:02.720
No way!

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:05.170
What the...

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:07.260
What the hell is going on?

00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:08.690
God damn!

00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:11.720
Even though I have reported so much!

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:14.390
What? Disbanded?

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:15.150
Yes.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:20.270
As of 23:59 today, our Willwears 
will be taken off-line,

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:23.310
and our access to the police 
network will be revoked.

00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:28.120
Once the paperwork is in order, 
we'll be transferred to the USDF.

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:30.450
Transferred? What's the meaning of this?

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:33.450
The only choice is to permit 
its continued existence!

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:36.210
I assume you've read my reports?!

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.520
I don't have that kind of time.

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:39.250
Huh?

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:42.730
I never needed your reports.

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:46.430
All I needed was the wearable device 
you were initially provided.

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:52.440
We were monitoring Unit 8 
24-7 through that device.

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:55.430
B-But that's spying!

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:57.470
Look who's talking.

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.650
You know what you agreed to do, right?

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:04.000
<i>Uploading!</i>

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:08.000
Well, now I can join in tonight's countdown.

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:09.530
Lucky me.

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:12.790
That's right. Projection mapping, was it?

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:14.870
What? Kyoukai-san?

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:17.070
Sorry. If we're disbanding,

00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:19.980
I have to deliver the Wear 
data to my headquarters.

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:22.000
I'm going home, too.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:23.120
See you.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:23.880
Hey!

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:24.920
Yeah?

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.720
On a day like this, at least...

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:29.190
At least what?

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:32.600
Wash out and toss your coffee can.

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:40.920
Asami-chan, I'm heading out.

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:44.190
Asami-chan?

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:52.220
For Sena, this place may have been a demotion.

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:55.200
But for me, it was a step up.

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:57.320
I had fun, too.

00:14:57.320 --> 00:14:59.020
I'm glad I met you all.

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:01.890
Hey, since we're parting ways,

00:15:02.190 --> 00:15:03.340
tell me your name.

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:07.000
Didn't I tell you before that it's Sado Namihei?

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:08.690
Yeah, right.

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:11.920
Well, I'll still be commuting to 
Kichijouji for a while,

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:13.180
so I'll see you around.

00:15:16.190 --> 00:15:19.250
I didn't hate this job.

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:22.670
I could feel I was keeping people safe.

00:15:23.050 --> 00:15:25.190
But what choice do we have?

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.950
You can't stop change.

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:28.990
Not in people, organizations, or cities.

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:31.660
Though, it is sad to see the unit shut down.

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:34.740
Yeah, to have it shut down...

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:40.000
<b>Refloat Waterfront 

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:43.170
<b>Notice of Closure</b>

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:45.880
Oh, come on. This place is closing, too?

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:54.180
Wait, why is it open?

00:16:06.870 --> 00:16:07.610
Hey!

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:10.730
Wh-Who are you?

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:12.500
That's my line.

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:15.860
This is private property. 
You'll be arrested for trespassing.

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:17.550
I'm the owner.

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:19.530
You're the one trespassing.

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:21.210
You're the owner?

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:23.390
You're lying. You're just a kid.

00:16:23.390 --> 00:16:25.530
Or are you the owner's kid?

00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:28.410
I'll show you the registration 
certificate if you'll leave.

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:30.370
I don't want to see that crap.

00:16:30.370 --> 00:16:31.090
Huh?

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.880
I just wanted to space out here.

00:16:34.730 --> 00:16:38.350
This was one of my go-to spots 
whenever I felt down.

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:43.180
Before, I was looking for a fight more 
than peace and quiet, though.

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:46.420
There was a scary guy named Inagi 
in my neighborhood

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:48.900
who was always on me for breaking the rules.

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:51.960
I'd get thrown into the electric bathtub a lot.

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:56.170
Terrible memories here, I guess.

00:16:56.760 --> 00:16:59.330
You don't look that peaceful right now, either.

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:00.300
But...

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:03.720
Whenever I came here, 
I'd feel like I could keep going.

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:07.530
And why are you here?

00:17:12.200 --> 00:17:13.350
To destroy.

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:14.060
Huh?

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:23.850
<b>Notice of Closure</b>

00:17:24.340 --> 00:17:25.600
How's it going?

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.360
Good, we're basically done.

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:28.350
I see.

00:17:28.350 --> 00:17:29.910
Soon, this place will be...

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:33.780
Then, to celebrate Kazari Asami's 
return to main headquarters,

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:34.820
cheers!

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:35.900
Cheers!

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:38.600
Now that Unit 8's gone,

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:41.810
you can hold your head high and go 
back to your elite career track.

00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:44.830
I was supposed to become the next

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:47.620
leader of Japan's ACTIVE Project...

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:49.090
But now...

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:54.080
I'd say that dream is still within your grasp.

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:56.790
B-But for the time being,

00:17:56.790 --> 00:17:59.510
I'll be sent to the Osaka or Aichi police force...

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:03.280
It's... It's my fault for being a spy...

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:05.560
Well, you didn't really end up spying on us.

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:07.490
I'm sorry.

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:09.790
It doesn't matter now.

00:18:09.790 --> 00:18:12.030
I'm used to the transfer switcheroo.

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:14.600
Right, you ended up here 
because of Bloody Mary...

00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:15.820
If I may...

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:19.930
I'm not hung up over Bloody Mary anymore.

00:18:19.930 --> 00:18:21.680
That's not what I'm talking about.

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:27.500
As the boss hypothesized, it makes more 
sense that there'd be one more in Logos.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:30.580
Then Hachijou's turning himself in was a ruse?

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:34.550
A ploy to buy time, in case the 
investigation might find them?

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:36.120
Why bother doing that?

00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:39.050
So there's a final plan?

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:42.260
And that will soon end...

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:44.350
They're not after money.

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:47.470
Don't you find it weird that 
Hachijou turned himself in?

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:50.060
What if they think they can get him out?

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:53.130
Either by breaking him out, 
or by getting him released...

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:56.020
They can't get him released 
without powerful connections...

00:18:56.020 --> 00:18:57.070
Oh!

00:18:57.640 --> 00:19:00.160
I have to go! It's almost time!

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:02.700
Oh, the projection mapping?

00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:06.980
<i>I wonder if this is how the</i>

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:09.010
<i>giant robot people felt, too.</i>

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:29.940
This is a pretty good spot.

00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:34.150
Let's just forget about everything 
and enjoy the countdown.

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:37.480
Less than a minute to go in the countdown!

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:39.360
Everyone ready?

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:40.610
Yeah!

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:44.660
<b>Sake 

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:50.160
<b>Sake 

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:52.120
Orochi...

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:53.000
Huh?

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:55.010
Orochi's...

00:19:55.010 --> 00:19:55.640
Ro?

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:58.380
The National Public Unified Intelligence Matrix.

00:19:58.380 --> 00:19:59.880
Thirty seconds!

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:04.380
The government acted during 
the hijacking case last year,

00:20:04.380 --> 00:20:07.100
and if we assume someone noticed...

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:10.860
To determine its undisclosed location 
and analyze government response,

00:20:10.860 --> 00:20:14.310
they triggered several 
seemingly unrelated crimes?

00:20:14.630 --> 00:20:15.520
Ten!

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:16.610
Nine!

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:17.570
It can't be...

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:18.320
Eight!

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:19.400
But if that's the case...

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:19.140
Seven!

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:20.490
Six!

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:21.570
Five!

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:22.780
Four!

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:23.860
Three!

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:23.860
Then...

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:24.950
Two!

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:26.030
One!

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:27.490
<b>Emergency Earthquake Alert</b>

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:29.160
<i>Emergency Earthquake Alert.</i>

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:31.070
<i>Please be prepared for a strong quake.</i>

00:20:31.070 --> 00:20:32.210
<i>Emergency Earthquake Alert.</i>

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.670
A-An earthquake?

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:36.030
<i>Prefectures projected to experience 
magnitude 7 earthquakes soon are:</i>

00:20:36.030 --> 00:20:38.130
<i>Kanagawa, Tokyo, Saitama,</i>

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:39.260
Magnitude 7?

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:40.590
<i>Ibaraki, Chiba, and Gunma.</i>

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:40.590
At a time like this?

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:44.010
<i>The earthquake is expected to 
happen at any moment.</i>

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:45.830
<i>Please go to a safe place.</i>

00:20:56.580 --> 00:20:58.400
What, it's not happening?

00:20:58.400 --> 00:20:59.310
Thank God.

00:20:59.310 --> 00:21:01.170
I was so nervous...

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:19.850
Prime Minister!

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:23.090
What in the world happened?

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:24.510
Did the seismometer malfunction?

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:26.300
We don't know the specifics,

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:29.180
but it seems someone breached 
the seismometer network.

00:21:29.180 --> 00:21:30.970
We believe that caused the malfunction.

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:33.040
Then fix it fast.

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:35.330
Talk about a bad omen during a rebuilding event.

00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:37.940
Prime Minister, we have an even bigger problem.

00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:41.720
The major earthquake alert triggered

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:45.420
a National Public Unified Intelligence 
Matrix failsafe system,

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:47.410
and someone's exploited a loophole.

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:48.870
What do you mean?

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:52.290
The administrator rights for Orochi's 
"O" and "chi" have been taken over,

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:55.580
and "ro" was automatically wiped 
due to the security protocol.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:56.340
Huh?

00:21:56.700 --> 00:21:57.850
Then you're saying...

00:21:58.170 --> 00:22:00.810
If we also lose admin access

00:22:00.810 --> 00:22:03.880
to the backup "ro"...

00:22:04.290 --> 00:22:07.660
We'll lose control over the entire 
government system in Japan?

00:22:15.930 --> 00:22:18.970
I shall be the one who rules.

00:23:50.070 --> 00:23:51.950
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:50.830 --> 00:23:52.180
Ohakonyapachininko!

00:23:51.950 --> 00:24:04.950
File 11: Japan Style

00:23:52.180 --> 00:23:53.630
We don't have time for this!

00:23:53.630 --> 00:23:54.990
What's going to happen to Unit 8?

00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:56.990
I still want to see everyone's exploits!

00:23:56.990 --> 00:23:58.100
Wait, what's that?

00:23:58.100 --> 00:23:59.200
Isn't that me?

00:23:59.200 --> 00:24:00.620
What's going on?

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:02.410
Next time, "Japan Style."

00:24:02.410 --> 00:24:04.360
What will happen to Japan?
